From 7d4631aab984ddfb1f6e8f30aba8c87c20397c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FEX-D2-reforged <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: cap pre-sleep and frame start pacing

Cap pre-sleep (VKD3D_FEX_PRESENT_PRESLEEP=1): a frame cap that sleeps
inside vkQueuePresentKHR (GameNative's FPS limit in its Vulkan layer)
sleeps while vkd3d holds the VkQueue that the game's compute and copy
queues share. Once presents are held at a steady period, sleep until
4 ms before the cap's next due time without the VkQueue.

Frame start pacing (VKD3D_FEX_FRAME_START=1): hold back the release of
the game's frame latency handle by the time its frames were measured to
wait anyway (queue thread wait plus the cap's hold, as far as the GPU
was done), minus a margin that grows when a frame comes late.

Both report into the FEX present timeline ('frame start', 'cap' lines).
